# go.env — Go toolchain wiring for the site-local cache (D41).
#
# Golden images (../../golden/) source these into the session environment (e.g.
# /etc/profile.d/ds-goproxy.sh, or `go env -w` baked at image build) so every
# session resolves Go modules through the pull-through cache. proxy.golang.org is
# reached ONLY on a cache miss, by the cache host. Nexus proxies; it implements
# no registry semantics (D41).
#
# Endpoint matches deploy/repos.yaml (go-proxy) and deploy/nexus.container :8081.
# `cache.ds.local` resolves in-VM to the cache host through the egress boundary
# allow-set (ds-dnsgate / ds-tlsproxy, D63).

# Resolve modules through the cache; `direct` fallback is intentionally OMITTED
# so a miss is served by the cache's upstream fetch, not a VM-direct egress that
# would bypass the boundary's registry allow-set.
GOPROXY=http://cache.ds.local:8081/repository/go-proxy/

# Module integrity stays ON. The Nexus go proxy serves the checksum-db
# passthrough, so GOSUMDB verification (sum.golang.org) rides through the cache.
GOSUMDB=sum.golang.org

# Do not bypass verification for any path by default; private-module exemptions,
# if ever needed, are an explicit per-org GONOSUMDB/GOPRIVATE addition.
GOFLAGS=-mod=mod
